<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0110a659087e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[8704] Pony.ai, a Chinese autonomous driving startup with an office in the U.S., has paused its driverless pilot fleet in California six months after it was approved by local regulators to test autonomous vehicles without a human safety driver." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8704" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/026592974f7b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "No fewer than 10 examples of the Hyundai Kona were previously registered under the driverless permit." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1518" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0af2b406f2d9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1516] Pony.ai, an autonomous vehicle startup based in Silicon Valley and Guangzhou, China, is temporarily unable to test driverless vehicles in California after a vehicle crash led the state’s Department of Motor Vehicles to suspend the company’s testing permit." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1516" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0b195989533e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Following an accident on October 28, 2021 while operating a vehicle in autonomous mode, Pony.ai‘s driverless testing permit has been suspended by the California Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8709" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/100e418dede3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1514] The suspension comes only six months after Pony.ai became the eighth company to receive a driverless testing permit in California, joining the likes of Alphabet Inc (GOOGL.O) unit Waymo as well as Cruise, backed by General Motors Co (GM.N)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1514" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/12d15534a0b8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[8709] Cruise, Nuro and Waymo are the only companies with permits allowing them to deploy autonomous vehicles in commercial operations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8709" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/148e7329be40> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Pony.AI is 1 of the few companies which has, and is using a permit from California to test vehicles with no safety driver on board at all." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1319" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/15d2a318607e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[8709] Cruise, Nuro and Waymo are the only companies with permits allowing them to deploy autonomous vehicles in commercial operations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8709" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/170862279481> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Pony.ai has subsequently worked with local authorities to resolve all issues related to the damaged sign." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8709" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/17fcd9f707bc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On November 19, the California Department of Motor Vehicles notified Pony.ai that it was suspending its driverless testing permit following a reported collision in Fremont on October 28, the DMV told TechCrunch in a statement." ;
