<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/06d3a6303f1f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Startup Pony.ai agrees to automated driving software recall" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1520" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0b4d08d39d58> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The agency said on Tuesday that this was the first recall of an automated driving system, Reuters first reported." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8708" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/11bc46e49137> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Pony.ai wants to roll out a robotaxi service in California next year, which is why the suspended permit is pretty troublesome for the American startup." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8706" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/152e9fa4fb33> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Pony.ai‘s driverless testing permit has been suspended by the California Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8709" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/153060694871> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to Pony.ai’s collision report, the incident took place on a clear morning when its driverless vehicle was changing lanes using the autonomous mode." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8704" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1f3b5ba8d30d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Report of Traffic Collision Involving an Autonomous Vehicle" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1513" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1f99f7be4328> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[8704] Pony.ai, a Chinese autonomous driving startup with an office in the U.S., has paused its driverless pilot fleet in California six months after it was approved by local regulators to test autonomous vehicles without a human safety driver." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8704" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/20f72eb8eb4c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Pony.ai, a Chinese autonomous driving startup with an office in the U.S., has paused its driverless pilot fleet in California six months after it was approved by local regulators to test autonomous vehicles without a human safety driver." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8704" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/21dac7b48a60> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "California suspends Pony.ai’s driverless testing after accident" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8709" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/26e433aea050> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Pony.ai suspension of driverless pilot in California" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8704" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/35055432702c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Startup technology firm Pony.ai agreed to issue a recall for some versions of its autonomous driving system software after an October crash in California, U.S. regulators said on Tuesday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1520" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/37a3b44992af> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "California suspends Pony.ai driverless test permit after crash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1517" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3b7277b5af56> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In addition to driverless technology, they also share missed targets and downsized plans." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8706" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3c62cd4b34e4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Toyota-backed Pony.ai had been testing its pilot fleet of 10 Hyundai Kona EVs without a human safety operator in California for several months when one of its vehicles collided with a lane divider and a street sign in Fremont." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8708" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4014aa57e46c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "California suspends Toyota-backed Pony.ai's driverless testing permit" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1515" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/45ba541c76dd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "While performing the lane change, the Pony.ai AV came into contact with a center divider on Fremont Blvd. and the traffic sign that was posted on the divider." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1513" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4a9ecb34d514> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "At-Fault Robotaxi Accidents For Waymo, Pony.AI, Olli And What They Mean For The Future" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1319" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/50ea541bf33f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Pony.ai’s permit to test driverless vehicles in California is suspended after crash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1516" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/55104797ec41> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1515] According to Reuters, the DMV suspended its driverless testing permit on November 19th, a few weeks after a reported collision in Fremont." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1515" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5d45a47518e2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On Oct. 28, a Pony.ai vehicle that had been operating in autonomous mode hit a street sign on a median in Fremont, California, after turning right, prompting California in December to suspend the company's driverless testing permit." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1520" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5d5d7b30e7e2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "California halts Pony.ai's driverless testing permit after accident" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1514" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5ff389a0eb4c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On October 28, 2021, after turning right onto Fremont Blvd from Cushing Pkwy, the Pony.ai Autonomous Vehicle (“Pony.ai AV”) performed a left lane change maneuver in autonomous mode." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1318" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/61c78f16fccd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Following an accident on October 28, 2021 while operating a vehicle in autonomous mode, Pony.ai‘s driverless testing permit has been suspended by the California Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1318" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/63619db0ce44> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The recall covers three vehicles that have been repaired, the company told the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1520" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6600e9e0825a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Founded in 2016 by Baidu veterans, Pony.ai is among a group of AV startups that have R&D teams and testing fleets in both China and California." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1517" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/66d32247e495> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Toyota-backed Pony.ai had been testing its pilot fleet of 10 Hyundai Kona EVs without a human safety operator in California for several months when one of its vehicles collided with a lane divider and a street sign in Fremont." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8708" .

